/target
/reference

# The generators import a helper from tools/, so running one leaves bytecode
# behind. Nothing here is worth keeping: it is per-interpreter, and there are
# already two versions of it from two Pythons.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# A cargo target directory built from a mangled absolute path. The scripts
# now refuse a relative CARGO_TARGET_DIR, which is what creates one; this is
# the second line of defence, because the first one was me.
/[A-Z]*Users*/
